# Preset: cg27a_kra44_pass1 - cg27a_kra43_pass1 on seed 4 (the real-text recipe's seed partner) + route J READOUTS: non-contrastive objective comparison, ensemble contradiction (4 seeds), latent program search. Readouts only.
# Preset: cg27a_kra43_pass1 - cg27a_kra41_pass1 + arrow premise rows x2 (inf_rchain_arrowprem 2) + 16 real-text rows a question step (inf_rchain_rows 16) + 400 test chains; no paraphrases (kra42's 13k premise rows diluted every premise). Seed 5.
# Preset: cg27a_kra41_pass1 - cg27a_kra36_pass1 + the STEP-1 FRAME on real text (inf_rchain_s1frame 1: 'A is within ' -> 'B >', the bridge retrieved in the chain's own context, C never shown) + the ANY VALID CHAIN readout. Seed 4 (as kra36).
# Preset: cg27a_kra36_pass1 - cg27a_kra35_pass1 + the ARROW PREMISE FRAME ('M > Z.' planted twice per rule-world premise, inf_rule_world_premarrow 2; real-text premises also taught as 'B > C.', inf_rchain_arrowprem 1): synthetic, 150 countries, new-bridge composition 0.49-0.52 -> 0.73-0.81 (roots never an answer 0.44-0.49 -> 0.65-0.77). Seed 4 (kra34's seed: kra34 = alignment without the frame).
# Preset: cg27a_kra35_pass1 - cg27a_kra34_pass1 + REAL-TEXT CHAINS with their own composite relation ('A is within B > C.', inf_rchain_crel; kra32: asked as 'A in ', the same prompt as a first premise worded 'in', test heads answered the premise and never chained, 0.01) and JEPA step-2 alignment on them (inf_rchain_align 0.5). Seed 5 (a second seed for kra34).
# Preset: cg27a_kra34_pass1 - cg27a_kra33_pass1 + JEPA STEP-2 ALIGNMENT (inf_rule_world_align 0.5: the state where 'A r2 B > ' predicts the root pulled to the bridge's own premise state 'B r1 ') + gate start-up floor 0.8 (inf_distill_gate_min). kra33 visit 5: pure families chain format 0.89, bridge 0.67, root 0.00 - the second step fails for bridges never in a chain; synthetic: step-2 alignment at the low dose 0.30 -> 0.65 (seed 0), equal (seed 1). Seed 4.
