# Preset: cg27a_kra29_pass1 - cg27a_kra28_pass1 with the ARROW chain form back ('X is a grandchild of M > Z.', inf_rule_world_chainplant 1) and the premises still in six wordings: the synthetic world composes through new bridges with the arrow form and varied premises (0.55-0.67) but not with the spelled form (0.12-0.14, second step fails; kra28 visit 3 the same). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra28_pass1 - cg27a_kra27_pass1 + the rule world's premises planted in six wordings (inf_rule_world_premw 6; knowledge augmentation: the synthetic world with ONE wording per premise composes through new bridges at 0.15-0.19 vs 0.55-0.67 with four, premises recalled 1.00 in both). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra27_pass1 - cg27a_kra26_pass1 with step 1 of the spelled composite WITHOUT the subject restated, 'X is a grandchild of: is a child of M; M is a child of Z.' (inf_rule_world_chainplant 3; kra26 at visit 3: pure families chain format 0.75 but bridge right 0.00 while the first step asked alone is right 0.66 - the stand-in cannot copy a new name). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra26_pass1 - cg27a_kra25_pass1 with the rule world's composites planted with both steps spelled, 'X is a grandchild of: X is a child of M; M is a child of Z.' (inf_rule_world_chainplant 2), route J writes taught directly (inf_distill_chainform 0). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra21_pass1 - cg27a_kra20_pass1 + confirmation by a top-quarter record (inf_rti_conf_q 0.75) + re-confirmation: retract confirmed inferences unrecorded 2 visits on (inf_rti_reconf 2). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra20_pass1 - cg27a_kra18_pass1 + confirmed inferences actually train the trunk (inf_kmc_useful 2) + a 0.25 floor on the question rows' decay; trained-count and broken-chain readouts. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra18_pass1 - cg27a_kra17_pass1 + name memory 1024 entries (was 384; conclusions had crowded out facts) + 8 question rows per step (was 4; facts faded as the pool grew). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra17_pass1 - cg27a_kra16_pass1 + a 0.125 floor on the question rows' visit decay (facts faded 0.88 -> 0.62 in kra14) + rated confirmation (only a record the seeded reader rates confirms). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra16_pass1 - cg27a_kra15_pass1 + inf_rti_chain 1 (MODEL CHANGE): confirmed inferences also taught after their premises (chain form), the composition step; readout REAL-TEXT INFERENCE IN CONTEXT. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra15_pass1 - cg27a_kra14_pass1 + inf_rti_nodecay 1 (MODEL CHANGE): confirmed real-text inferences' dose rows exempt from the question rows' visit decay, the cause of their fading on the A6 stand-in (0.724 -> 0.316). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra14_pass1 - cg27a_kra13_pass1 + the SEEDED READER (20,000 labelled records with context words replace the label-free teacher; ReVerb, multi-instance and knowledge teaching off). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra13_pass1 - cg27a_kra12_pass1 + wider records, the compressed fact table from the reader's top half (MODEL CHANGE), the reader taught by confirmed inferences + ReVerb phrases + multi-instance, the after-gate made-up readout. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra12_pass1 - cg27a_kra11_pass1 + CONFIRM, CONSOLIDATE, FADE (inf_rti_tentative 1; MODEL CHANGE): real-text inferences tentative until a later relational record confirms them; only confirmed ones are taught and enter the memory; unconfirmed fade after 4 visits. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra11_pass1 - cg27a_kra10_pass1 + the premise-update fix (inf_nm_update_first 1) + route J on every recorded fact (inf_kmc_rulej_allrec 1) (MODEL CHANGES) + the END-TO-END real-text readout (inf_premises_e2e 1). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra10_pass1 - cg27a_kra9_pass1 + the STATE READER readout (inf_premises_states 6000): the usefulness-taught reader on the trunk's own states, repeated at each premises readout; + the PARSER reader readout (inf_premises_parse 4000; spaCy, by the user's decision). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra9_pass1 - cg27a_kra8_pass1 + premise change in the rule world (15% of held-back leaves move) + route J belief revision: recency and re-derive/rewrite every write each sleep (MODEL CHANGES) + self-trained wording reader readout. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra8_pass1 - cg27a_kra7_pass1 + source replay doubled (16) + readouts: substitution reader on the benchmark records, made-up chains after chain-form teaching. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra6_pass1 - cg27a_kra5_pass1 with ROUTE J (JEPA-style relational memory: latent operators composed via the learned rule) and its gated writes replacing route D's. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra5_pass1 - cg27a_kra4_pass1 + route D abstention (inf_kmc_rulecomp_dgate 1) + source replay 8 (TWO model changes, by the user's decision); premise readouts. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra4_pass1 - cg27a_krd_pass1 + ROUTE D WRITES with their gate (inf_kmc_rulecomp_dwrite 1; MODEL CHANGE). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_krd_pass1 - cg27a_kra_pass1 + the ROUTE D readout (inf_kmc_rulecomp_decode 100; readout only): the trunk decodes two steps via the learned rule. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kra_pass1 - cg27a_kcr3_pass1 + the ROUTE A readout (inf_kmc_rulecomp 2; readout only, no model change): composition by two reads of the integrated memory. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kcr3_pass1 - cg27a_kcr2 + pure test families (no composite planted in half the rule-world families). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kus_pass1 - cg27a_kty_pass1 + THE USEFULNESS KEEP RULE (inf_kmc_useful 1; ONE model change): judged AND useful inferences reach the trunk. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kty_pass1 - cg27a_kmr_pass1 + TYPED WRITES (inf_rti_typed 1; ONE model change): written inferences as 'head <wording> tail' instead of
# 'A is connected to C'. Gate rule off (readout compares); keyed continuation units ride along (prediction time only). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmr_pass1 - cg27a_kmf_pass1 + THE RELATIONAL-RECORDS JUDGE (inf_rret_sig rel; ONE model change): consolidation and retraction judged by the
# records that link the pair by words, not lists. Readouts: the gate rule (untyped inferences' slots shut on text), all judge signals. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmf_pass1 - cg27a_kmt_pass1's model, READOUTS ONLY: memory feedback from reading (inf_kmfb 1) and two-hop with a memory-only hop. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmt_pass1 - cg27a_kmb_pass1 + A STRICTER GATE (inf_kmi_gatew 0.85; ONE model change): the all-text memory's cost on Wikipedia text. Readouts:
# relation types from the trunk and typed rules over them (inf_rtype), two-hop through the memory, stricter-gate bits. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmb_pass1 - cg27a_kma_pass1 + RECONSOLIDATION-STYLE RETRACTION (inf_kmc_mode byte; ONE model change): a retracted inference's own answer
# bytes lowered in the slots it reads, nothing else; recorded so it can be undone. Readouts: inferences by consolidation status and age, learning speed as a judge. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kma_pass1 - cg27a_kmc_pass1 + THE ALL-TEXT ADDRESS (inf_kma 1; ONE model change): the keyed memory addressed at every byte of any text
# from the trunk's own forward (subject identity hash x in-context JEPA wording key x name byte), read on all text through the gate (0.7), written
# on answer bytes only; 256 x 256 slots. Readout: prequential bits with the memory. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmc_pass1 - cg27a_kmg_pass1 + CONSOLIDATION THROUGH THE MEMORY (inf_kmc 1, judge inf_rret 1 with signal 'docs'; ONE model change): written
# inferences teach the keyed memory at once and the trunk only once judged on later reading and kept; flagged ones are counter-written out of the memory. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmg_pass1 - cg27a_kmi_pass1 + THE GATE (inf_kmi_gate 1; ONE model change): the integrated keyed memory answers only where its address
# was written; readouts: abstention on never-read names, counter-write retraction (oracle, on a copy). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_kmi_pass1 - cg27a_rasymaa_pass1 + THE INTEGRATED KEYED MEMORY (inf_kmi 1; ONE model change): the question rows read a keyed memory
# (subject-name identity key x JEPA wording key x answer byte) where their answers are predicted, its logits added to the trunk's; it learns from
# those rows with the trunk's logits detached (trunk training unchanged). The keyed memory readout (inf_kmem) rides along. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rasymaa_pass1 - cg27a_rasym_pass1 + CODE + ADAMIC-ADAR UNDER THE ASYMMETRY FILTER (inf_rcode_sel code+aa; ONE model change): the GPU
# readout put code + AA above code + RA among asymmetric pairs at every write (top 200: 0.74 / 0.70 / 0.73 vs 0.68 / 0.67 / 0.70). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rasym_pass1 - cg27a_rcode5_pass1 + ASYMMETRY FILTER (inf_rcode_asym 1.0; ONE model change): write only pairs whose names differ
# clearly in how general they are (|log degree ratio| > 1). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rcode5_pass1 - cg27a_rcode4_pass1 + DOSE SCALING (inf_rti_rows_ref 8; ONE model change): each of the 16 dose rows pushes as hard as
# one of cg27a_rcode3's 8 (cg27a_rcode4 halved it: the dose loss is a mean over its rows). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rcode4_pass1 - cg27a_rcode3_pass1 + WRITE TWICE AS MANY (inf_rcode_sel code+ra, inf_rti_max 200, inf_rti_rows 16; ONE model change): the 200
# pairs the code and resource allocation agree on most, each with cg27a_rcode3's rows. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rcode3_pass1 - cg27a_rcode2_pass1 + SELECTION (inf_rcode_sel code+aa, inf_rti_max 100; ONE model change): write the 100 pairs the compressed
# code and chaining agree on most. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rcode2_pass1 - cg27a_rcode_pass1 + RTI DOSE (inf_rti_rows 8; ONE model change): written real-text inferences get their own question rows,
# 8 per step; rank-recall readout. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rcode_pass1 - cg27a_rti_pass1 + INFERENCE BY COMPRESSING THE FACT TABLE (inf_rti_code 1; ONE model change): low-rank name codes of the
# store's record graph choose which never-stated pairs to write as inferences. A third held back. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rti_pass1 - END-TO-END REAL-TEXT INFERENCE: cg27a_xgain_pass1 + the PREMISES store + ONE model change (inf_rti_write 1): label-free
# premises -> A-C through a shared name (2+ bridges) -> checked by the trunk -> written into the question pool (a fifth held back). Surprise gate off. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_prem_pass1 - cg27a_xgain_pass1 + THE SURPRISE-GATED STORE (inf_sstore 1; ONE model change): real-text sentences enter the fast store
# only if the trunk finds them surprising; + the PREMISES AT SCALE readout (inf_premises 1): a separate record store reads the DocRED distant set
# (the notebook downloads it) - types by record compression, trunk surprise, premise precision and A-C inference by policy. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_xgain_pass1 - cg27a_rtxw_pass1 + the EXTRACTION GAIN readout (inf_extract_gain 1; readout only, no model change): does a candidate
# record from real text save the trunk bits where its names meet again, more for related pairs? Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtxw_pass1 - cg27a_rtxt_pass1 + REAL-TEXT REPLAY THROUGH THE WIKIPEDIA SLOT (inf_distill_rtx_slot 1; one change): the forgetting fix
# (cg27a_rtxt: forgetting +0.077 vs +0.026; Gutenberg +0.224). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtxt_pass1 - cg27a_rtx16_pass1 + TITLE FOR PRONOUN (inf_distill_rtx_title 1; one change): pronoun-led replayed real sentences replayed
# with the document's title for the pronoun. Named sentences confirm the real-text result to visit 10. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtx16_pass1 - cg27a_rtx_pass1 with four times the real-text replay (inf_distill_rtx 16; one change). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rtx_pass1 - cg27a_replay_pass1 + REAL-TEXT REPLAY of half the benchmark documents as plain text, NO view alignment
# (inf_distill_rtx 4, inf_distill_rtx_align 0; one change: replay is the single cause). The test: real-text recall from the weights, replayed vs control documents. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_replay_pass1 - cg27a_align_pass1 + SOURCE REPLAY (inf_distill_replay 4; ONE model change): the stored source sentences of the
# question pool's facts and of the never-asked control fifth replayed as plain text with every question-row step. The test: the trunk
# completes control facts' own sentences (cg27a_align 0.00) and then answers them in the test wordings (never asked). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_align_pass1 - cg27a_rwclean_pass1 + VIEW ALIGNMENT (inf_distill_align 0.5; ONE model change, after LLM-JEPA): each taught
# question row's state at the answer is pulled toward the state where the fact's own source sentence predicts the answer (a stop-gradient
# target). The test is the never-taught CONTROL fifth in the test wordings (facts the trunk only READ). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rwclean_pass1 - cg27a_chunk_pass1 + the clean step-4 control (inf_rw_nosleep 1: the rule world's two-hop pairs are never
# concluded by the sleep layer, so composites reach the trunk only through the relational module's write). Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_chunk_pass1 - cg27a_relwrite_pass1 (step 4, the same one model change) + the FAST SEQUENCE CHANNEL READER as readouts
# (inf_reader_chunk 1: a separate evidence record scored against the gold relations; the relational module on real text). The step-4 readout
# now also reports recall with the closed-form edits subtracted. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_relwrite_pass1 - cg27a_relmod_pass1 (with the fixed relational module) + STEP 4: its verified conclusions WRITTEN into the
# distillation question pool (inf_distill_relmod_write 1; ONE model change). The test: the trunk recalls composite facts never planted. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_relmod_pass1 - cg27a_rag_pass1 + the RELATIONAL MODULE readout (inf_distill_relmod 1500; step 3 of the rule test): rules discovered
# from the reader's facts against a shuffled null and a functional check, typed conclusions proposed and scored, nothing written. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_rag_pass1 - the new defaults (= cg27a_distillcap_pass1, plus the RULE WORLD) + retrieval-augmented answers with cited sources,
# latent chaining and operator algebra on the rule world (readouts; no model change). Seed 4 (the notebook's SEED line must be 4).
# Preset: cg27a_distillcap_pass1 - cg27a_distillm_pass1 with the question pool beyond the name memory's cap (inf_distill_pool_max 2000; ONE model change),
# the ever-taught ledger readout and the store-write stage memory marks. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_distillm_pass1 - cg27a_distillw_pass1 with the question rows restricted to the blocks' mlp_out weights (ONE model change), the
# Gaussian drift readout, per-phase GPU peaks and cache release, memory guard 0.6. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_distillw_pass1 - cg27a_carry_pass1 + INTERLEAVED DISTILLATION (inf_distill_wake 0.25: 4 question rows about stored facts in every
# real-text training step, same backward and optimiser; a fifth of the facts never taught). The sleep burst (inf_distill) stays off. Seed 4.
# Preset: cg27a_carry_pass1 - cg27a_readouts_pass1 + CARRY THE SUBJECT (inf_carry 0.1: an auxiliary loss teaching the trunk to keep the latest
# name readable at the bytes after it; the test is the [SLOT CARRIES THE SUBJECT?] readout every third sleep). Seed 4, as the run without it.
# Preset: cg27a_readouts_pass1 - the current build (cg27a, self-contrast on) with every 9 Nov readout: answer-slot gates, system-written question forms
# in the shadow edits, ROME-style fit diagnostic, latent judge hard controls, sticky routing, sleep phases, ceiling tests last. Seed 3: a third seed.
# Preset: cg27a_pass1 - cg27a for pass 1 only (10 visits, about 2 hours; the end-of-run readouts come after visit 10). cg27a = cg26z (closed loop with hints, the store reads the text) + the write side: conclusions in several wordings, competitor contrast, information-weighted answer bytes, closed-form edits on three wordings (branch cg27a)
# The JEPA index trains its own small text encoder on the stored sentences each sleep and reports retrieval,
# one-hop with the retrieved sentence in context and two-hop by retrieval; cg26u adds two more encoder arms
# (C: InfoNCE; G: names masked, a generic trace), routing of each visit by bytes and by JEPA codes, and where
# the replay teacher signal sits by byte class. All readouts: the trunk and the router are not changed by them.
# Build: the platypus package (python -m platypus).
# Clean evaluation is the build's default: oracle options off (REM subjects
# not drawn from the planted probe facts, dream cues not chosen by benchmark
# gold entities, JEPA batches not balanced by the planted label), held-out
# probe wordings with the bridge among the candidates and no slot given,
# schema fit measured with its own prompt. PLATYPUS_CLEAN=0 restores cg26p.

PRESET_BUILD=platypus
PRESET_SEED=5

PLATYPUS_CLEAN=1

# Conduit hints in the closed-loop passes (true bytes given to the generator).
# 1 = as cg26p; 0 = none (the strict closed loop; GPU cg26w: 0.87-0.99 of replay rebuilt exactly).
PLATYPUS_HINTS=1

# Closed-form edits (re-solve every sleep). 0 turns them off.
PLATYPUS_CF=1

# Sleep schedule: adaptive (default since cg26n) or fixed.
PLATYPUS_SLEEP=adaptive

PLATYPUS_DREAMS=jepa
PLATYPUS_RULEFREE=1
PLATYPUS_ROUTEFIX=1
PLATYPUS_PASSES=1
PILE_CACHE=pile_cache
FLA_AUTO_INSTALL=1

# PLATYPUS_SLOTS=N would let the router open up to N slots (more than the
# number of domains); locally every revisit then went to a new slot, so the
# cap stays until the router recognises revisits by itself.

# Function timer: 1 prints the seconds spent in each sleep, readout and
# diagnostic function after every visit and for the whole run (adds a GPU
# synchronisation per call, so a little slower). Off by default.
PLATYPUS_FNTIME=0

# The JEPA index, routing and byte-class readout options.
LAB_OVR_FILE=configs/presets/cg27a_kra60.overrides.json
